WEBVTT

00:00:04.850 --> 00:00:09.320
Labor: A robot specifically designed
for construction work.

00:00:09.940 --> 00:00:12.610
Labors allow dramatic advances
in construction...

00:00:12.610 --> 00:00:14.320
but also in crime.

00:00:14.660 --> 00:00:16.570
To combat these
new Labor crimes...

00:00:16.700 --> 00:00:20.240
the police created a special unit:
The Patrol Labor.

00:00:20.540 --> 00:00:23.160
And thus, the birth of Patlabor.

00:00:49.230 --> 00:00:51.820
yume wo sutenaide
You must not let go of your dreams

00:00:52.070 --> 00:00:54.610
me wo sorasanaide
And never turn your gaze away

00:00:55.610 --> 00:00:59.620
futari no ai mo kumoru yo
Yet even still love may cloud up and fade away

00:01:01.120 --> 00:01:04.000
utsumuita kata wo
And even though you comforted your love

00:01:04.120 --> 00:01:07.000
dakishimeta keredo
When he was feeling down

00:01:07.580 --> 00:01:11.840
samishisa mune ni tsumotta
Sadness was still weighing down his heavy heart

00:01:13.300 --> 00:01:19.050
yume wa kimi no buki no hazu da yo
Hang on tight to your dreams - they're weapons in your arsenal

00:01:19.260 --> 00:01:25.640
nee da kara kanashimi mo kinukete itte
You'll find that you can get through anything at all

00:01:26.270 --> 00:01:31.980
so never cry itsu mo kimi wo mitsumete 'ru yo
So never cry - you know I will always be watching over you

00:01:32.820 --> 00:01:37.780
fair na ikikata no kimi ga suki
What I love about you is your strong sense of fairness

00:01:38.320 --> 00:01:44.330
so never cry itsu mo kimi no soba ni iru yo
So never cry - you know I will always be right there by your side

00:01:45.120 --> 00:01:50.000
da kara mata asu e kakedashite
And so now you can face your future fearlessly

00:01:57.840 --> 00:02:01.850
Ota's Afternoon of Puzzlement

00:02:03.810 --> 00:02:04.810
Ota is meeting...

00:02:05.560 --> 00:02:06.640
A potential fiancée?

00:02:07.850 --> 00:02:10.190
What's she like?

00:02:11.360 --> 00:02:13.320
Feast your eyes!

00:02:14.480 --> 00:02:15.530
Is she a human?

00:02:18.450 --> 00:02:20.570
Oh, my god!
She's beautiful!

00:02:20.740 --> 00:02:22.320
Break up with her!

00:02:22.320 --> 00:02:24.200
I'll steal her away!

00:02:25.790 --> 00:02:28.330
Stop it, Shige!

00:02:28.370 --> 00:02:29.540
Shut up!

00:02:41.050 --> 00:02:42.600
This is my nephew,
Isao Ota.

00:02:43.180 --> 00:02:46.430
He's employed with
the police department.

00:02:46.810 --> 00:02:48.310
Ota, this is Ayano Fujii.

00:02:50.020 --> 00:02:51.810
I'm Ayano Fujii.

00:02:52.060 --> 00:02:54.900
Pleased to meet you.

00:02:56.690 --> 00:02:58.320
Please pardon my nephew.

00:02:58.360 --> 00:03:01.110
His police work has left him a
little rough around the edges.

00:03:09.080 --> 00:03:10.500
It's hot!

00:03:10.620 --> 00:03:12.370
Oh dear...

00:03:14.540 --> 00:03:17.210
Are you all right?
You didn't get wet, did you?

00:03:17.500 --> 00:03:21.180
No, no! I'm fine,
thank you!

00:03:23.640 --> 00:03:25.390
Well, shall we?

00:03:25.640 --> 00:03:27.930
Let's give them
some time together.

00:03:28.390 --> 00:03:30.680
Ayano, would you care
for a walk in their garden?

00:03:32.060 --> 00:03:34.650
Isao, why don't you
show her around?

00:03:47.530 --> 00:03:51.250
Oh, my leg's asleep!
Sorry!

00:04:09.010 --> 00:04:10.600
Good morning!

00:04:18.980 --> 00:04:22.320
Ota, do you have a cold?
Oh, how was yesterday's...?

00:04:22.360 --> 00:04:24.990
Noa!
We need some tea.

00:04:26.990 --> 00:04:29.910
He fell into the pond?
Right in front of her?

00:04:30.740 --> 00:04:32.000
Quiet!

00:04:32.200 --> 00:04:34.250
But it's too cold
to look at ponds!

00:04:34.370 --> 00:04:37.580
He probably wasn't paying
attention, and slipped.

00:04:37.880 --> 00:04:39.880
I think he blew it.

00:04:39.960 --> 00:04:40.960
Oh, no!

00:04:41.550 --> 00:04:43.380
So the words "arranged
marriage" are taboo!

00:04:43.720 --> 00:04:45.550
Also: Rejection,
catastrophe, refusal,

00:04:46.800 --> 00:04:52.560
break up, destroy, fall, fall into,
slip, garden lantern, goldfish.

00:04:52.560 --> 00:04:57.980
Anything associated with
ponds is out. Got it?

00:05:00.150 --> 00:05:03.610
Here's your tea, Ota!

00:05:03.820 --> 00:05:06.450
It's on the edge,
so don't let it fall...

00:05:06.610 --> 00:05:10.240
Oh, Ota! Your Ingram will
be fixed this afternoon!

00:05:10.330 --> 00:05:11.700
They fixed everything
you broke up...

00:05:14.200 --> 00:05:14.750
Yes?

00:05:18.540 --> 00:05:20.960
Ota, it's for you.
It's your aunt.

00:05:23.760 --> 00:05:26.260
Isao here. Yes.

00:05:27.760 --> 00:05:29.850
Yes. Yes.

00:05:38.350 --> 00:05:45.190
Ota, it really has more to do
with luck than with love.

00:05:45.190 --> 00:05:49.240
Yeah, someone better
will come along!

00:05:49.370 --> 00:05:50.910
Someone who
appreciates your charm!

00:05:52.370 --> 00:05:55.830
Beauty really IS in the
eye of the beholder!

00:05:56.870 --> 00:06:02.090
She'll meet me at 7 tomorrow
in the Imperial Hotel lobby.

00:06:12.100 --> 00:06:14.140
What are you doing here?

00:06:14.350 --> 00:06:15.470
Nothing, really.

00:06:15.930 --> 00:06:19.690
What's going on with Division 2?
Even the mechanics are helping.

00:06:20.270 --> 00:06:21.110
Are you having
a meeting?

00:06:21.980 --> 00:06:26.570
They're working
on a special case.

00:06:27.490 --> 00:06:28.780
What?

00:06:30.110 --> 00:06:31.740
No, that sounds too trite.

00:06:32.070 --> 00:06:37.330
What if she hates baseball?
A movie would be safer.

00:06:37.410 --> 00:06:40.040
Did you learn what
her hobbies are?

00:06:40.210 --> 00:06:43.250
Yeah, if you don't know that,
you can't plan a strategy.

00:06:43.540 --> 00:06:46.710
I guess we'll just have to
move on to technique.

00:06:47.260 --> 00:06:50.050
When you see her,
you MUST praise her clothes.

00:06:50.260 --> 00:06:52.680
That supercedes all
details of technique.

00:06:53.100 --> 00:06:56.470
Excellent! Input from an
actual female! Anything else?

00:06:56.810 --> 00:07:00.940
NEVER be late! And if you're
on time but she was early,

00:07:01.270 --> 00:07:03.900
you still have to apologize.
It's an iron-clad rule.

00:07:06.940 --> 00:07:09.360
Shut up!
What do you think this is?

00:07:09.610 --> 00:07:10.360
Huh?

00:07:10.900 --> 00:07:13.320
It's your first date, Ota.

00:07:20.910 --> 00:07:22.000
I'm late! I'm late!

00:07:27.500 --> 00:07:28.460
She's already here!

00:07:30.260 --> 00:07:33.260
One: Apologize!
Two: Praise clothes.

00:07:46.110 --> 00:07:49.780
Hello! It's beautiful
that I made you late!

00:07:51.280 --> 00:07:55.620
Uh, no. Hello! I'm sorry
that you look beautiful!

00:07:58.410 --> 00:08:02.160
I just got here,
and thank you.

00:08:10.340 --> 00:08:13.510
Sleet. Are you warm enough?

00:08:13.720 --> 00:08:18.010
I'm fine.
I like the sleet.

00:08:18.430 --> 00:08:21.730
I love the possibility that it may
become a beautiful snowfall.

00:08:27.610 --> 00:08:30.980
Idiot! Adjust speed
for road conditions!

00:08:31.150 --> 00:08:33.110
They'll splash you if you stay
on that side. Come over here!

00:08:34.820 --> 00:08:38.620
Oh, I'm sorry, I'm sorry!
I'll wipe it off.

00:08:38.700 --> 00:08:40.330
It's nothing, really.

00:08:42.700 --> 00:08:46.290
I'm afraid
you're just spreading it.

00:08:48.340 --> 00:08:50.380
Oh, I'm terribly sorry!

00:08:56.340 --> 00:08:57.550
Ota!

00:08:58.760 --> 00:08:59.810
Ota!

00:09:01.140 --> 00:09:02.640
The meeting has started.

00:09:03.770 --> 00:09:04.730
Ota!

00:09:05.560 --> 00:09:08.690
Oh, Izumi.
Give that to me.

00:09:11.070 --> 00:09:12.860
No, that's okay.

00:09:13.190 --> 00:09:14.360
Give me that.

00:09:15.360 --> 00:09:17.990
Women shouldn't
do heavy work.

00:09:19.950 --> 00:09:24.200
Izumi, do you love the
possibility of a snowfall?

00:09:25.790 --> 00:09:28.670
I was awake all night
thinking about that.

00:09:30.500 --> 00:09:31.590
I see.

00:09:36.840 --> 00:09:40.510
The only current investigation
is an engineering disaster:

00:09:40.640 --> 00:09:43.220
A Labor that's
too heavy to move.

00:09:43.680 --> 00:09:46.020
I'm sorry.
I didn't mean to bore you.

00:09:46.310 --> 00:09:50.020
No, I'm the one who asked.

00:09:50.310 --> 00:09:51.570
Oh, good.

00:09:51.900 --> 00:09:54.440
Shall we get some tea?

00:09:54.480 --> 00:09:57.240
I'd like to go
somewhere else, first.

00:09:57.700 --> 00:09:58.110
Where?

00:10:02.830 --> 00:10:03.330
There.

00:10:04.660 --> 00:10:08.080
Since you're in Patlabor,
you must know all about it.

00:10:08.330 --> 00:10:11.710
I'm not familiar with it.
It's a new model.

00:10:11.960 --> 00:10:15.420
Hishii Industries released it
just last month.

00:10:16.720 --> 00:10:20.220
Movement precision is 20%
above any similar model.

00:10:20.550 --> 00:10:22.470
Still, it's very light
for its size.

00:10:22.970 --> 00:10:26.020
There are only two in use
in the entire country.

00:10:26.390 --> 00:10:27.230
It's so pretty.

00:10:28.520 --> 00:10:30.440
The Labor?

00:10:30.690 --> 00:10:35.610
Isn't it beautiful?
I love Labors.

00:10:36.110 --> 00:10:40.240
Labors that work in the dark,
or up so high.

00:10:43.660 --> 00:10:45.200
He's acting weird.

00:10:45.330 --> 00:10:48.910
I agree. It's creepy,
just sitting next to him.

00:10:49.670 --> 00:10:51.880
Ota is a prisoner of love!

00:10:52.500 --> 00:10:53.880
She's beautiful.

00:10:54.290 --> 00:10:57.880
One simple question:
What does she see in Ota?

00:11:00.630 --> 00:11:02.720
His easy-to-understand
personality!

00:11:03.390 --> 00:11:05.890
- That's not a compliment.
- You're right.

00:11:06.260 --> 00:11:08.100
He has a
strong sense of justice.

00:11:08.560 --> 00:11:10.270
Although he can be
rather violent.

00:11:12.810 --> 00:11:14.110
I want to talk to you!

00:11:14.230 --> 00:11:18.530
I didn't say anything!
Really!

00:11:20.070 --> 00:11:21.490
Please, you have to tell me!

00:11:22.700 --> 00:11:27.950
I'm raising a dog.
A woman says, "Oh, I love the dog!"

00:11:27.990 --> 00:11:28.950
What does it mean?

00:11:29.250 --> 00:11:31.420
What, you don't like dogs?

00:11:32.500 --> 00:11:33.830
You blockhead!

00:11:34.130 --> 00:11:38.420
She knows I pilot a Patlabor!
And she says, "Oh, I love Labors!"

00:11:38.590 --> 00:11:41.880
Is she showing that
she's interested in me?

00:11:42.220 --> 00:11:45.350
Or at least
she doesn't hate you.

00:11:45.760 --> 00:11:46.970
Got it!

00:11:53.600 --> 00:11:55.690
Charging off again.

00:12:07.990 --> 00:12:10.330
- Would you like one?
- Yes, please.

00:12:19.630 --> 00:12:21.510
I know this is sudden...

00:12:22.470 --> 00:12:25.720
I don't mean to rush things...

00:12:28.140 --> 00:12:30.680
We only met
a short time ago.

00:12:31.020 --> 00:12:34.900
But we haven't discussed
an important topic yet.

00:12:36.190 --> 00:12:41.690
I'm not sure how to say this,
so let me be direct, Ayano.

00:12:41.690 --> 00:12:42.400
I'm sorry.

00:12:43.740 --> 00:12:47.570
I... I'm sorry.

00:12:47.740 --> 00:12:51.500
This won't work.
I'm really sorry.

00:12:56.080 --> 00:12:57.000
Ayano!

00:13:01.510 --> 00:13:05.510
Phantom

00:13:07.510 --> 00:13:10.510
XR-99 Ivan

00:13:21.150 --> 00:13:22.860
Ota, aren't you having lunch?

00:13:23.150 --> 00:13:26.660
You can have half of mine.
You need the energy!

00:13:26.660 --> 00:13:27.990
Ota!

00:13:28.780 --> 00:13:33.370
It's target practice time! I heard
they're using live ammo today!

00:13:33.830 --> 00:13:36.370
Really?
That's great, isn't it, Ota?

00:13:40.670 --> 00:13:41.500
Ota?

00:13:41.960 --> 00:13:43.210
I can get lunch for you!

00:13:47.470 --> 00:13:51.050
He ignored both
lunch and target practice.

00:13:51.180 --> 00:13:55.390
He wasn't used to flying,
so his crash was even harder.

00:13:57.770 --> 00:13:58.770
What do you mean?

00:13:59.520 --> 00:14:02.730
Her parents must
have pushed the issue.

00:14:03.280 --> 00:14:04.730
Do people still do that?

00:14:05.400 --> 00:14:08.200
I don't know. He said
she had a lot of good qualities.

00:14:08.450 --> 00:14:11.910
But then she dumped him.
She should have spoken up earlier.

00:14:12.240 --> 00:14:13.910
I think she was pressured.

00:14:14.200 --> 00:14:16.410
So you're taking her side.

00:14:25.170 --> 00:14:26.550
Excuse me...

00:14:26.800 --> 00:14:29.720
What's wrong, ma'am?
Are you lost?

00:14:30.090 --> 00:14:33.680
Oh, no.
Is Isao Ota here?

00:14:34.470 --> 00:14:38.350
Oh, so you're...

00:14:38.890 --> 00:14:41.980
I'll call him! OTA!

00:14:48.900 --> 00:14:51.030
It isn't right to spy on people.

00:14:51.240 --> 00:14:53.530
You should talk!
You're hiding, too.

00:14:53.950 --> 00:14:55.950
I'm just worried.

00:14:56.200 --> 00:14:57.790
They're leaving!

00:15:08.760 --> 00:15:09.930
Are you cold?

00:15:10.260 --> 00:15:11.680
I'm fine.

00:15:17.060 --> 00:15:19.890
I'm sorry to barge in
on you like this.

00:15:20.020 --> 00:15:21.980
It's nothing.

00:15:22.520 --> 00:15:27.150
I had to talk to you.
There's something I have to say.

00:15:28.690 --> 00:15:32.950
I know it's too late,
but I have to tell you.

00:15:33.240 --> 00:15:35.830
I've never told this to anyone.

00:15:36.120 --> 00:15:39.250
I took advantage of you, but...

00:15:39.870 --> 00:15:40.620
Snow.

00:15:41.750 --> 00:15:43.250
We're going to have a snowfall.

00:15:53.340 --> 00:15:54.220
Ayano...

00:15:57.680 --> 00:16:00.350
Excuse me...
that's the order to mobilize.

00:16:09.360 --> 00:16:10.690
Sorry, but it sounds serious.

00:16:10.940 --> 00:16:13.820
What is it? More terrorists?
A rampaging Labor?

00:16:14.200 --> 00:16:17.780
No, the new bullet
train subway collapsed.

00:16:18.870 --> 00:16:21.370
Hishii's newest Labor
has been buried alive.

00:16:22.210 --> 00:16:23.330
Hishii's new Labor?

00:16:23.960 --> 00:16:26.250
Not in Shinjuku!

00:16:26.710 --> 00:16:30.130
Oh, hello. Do you have
some interest in this?

00:16:30.260 --> 00:16:34.090
Excuse me, I know
this is a selfish request,

00:16:34.470 --> 00:16:37.970
but please let me come.
Let me see the scene.

00:16:38.350 --> 00:16:38.970
Ayano...

00:16:41.180 --> 00:16:44.190
Okay, you can come with us.

00:16:45.600 --> 00:16:46.440
Oh, thank you!

00:16:50.980 --> 00:16:52.570
What's the situation?

00:16:52.780 --> 00:16:55.490
The cave-in is worse
than we thought.

00:16:55.530 --> 00:16:57.370
We can't use
construction Labors.

00:16:57.990 --> 00:16:59.990
What about the trapped Labor?

00:17:00.080 --> 00:17:02.000
We think his radio is out.

00:17:02.200 --> 00:17:04.660
He's been silent since
the accident, an hour ago.

00:17:05.080 --> 00:17:06.830
Do you know the
name of the pilot?

00:17:07.210 --> 00:17:07.920
Yes.

00:17:09.290 --> 00:17:11.710
Takaaki Ichihara,
27 years old.

00:17:12.550 --> 00:17:16.300
He's a contractor with over two
years' experience piloting Labors.

00:17:18.050 --> 00:17:18.640
Ayano!

00:17:19.680 --> 00:17:21.810
- I'm sorry.
- What's wrong?

00:17:21.850 --> 00:17:23.100
Ota, move it!

00:17:23.480 --> 00:17:24.520
I'm coming!

00:17:25.190 --> 00:17:28.020
Go rest in the car.
You look pale.

00:17:28.100 --> 00:17:29.940
- But...
- Please do it.

00:17:36.780 --> 00:17:38.950
It's claustrophobic in here.

00:17:46.250 --> 00:17:46.920
Around here.

00:17:52.130 --> 00:17:56.090
Start immediately.
The pilot's running out of time.

00:17:56.220 --> 00:17:58.220
We understand.
Let's go, Izumi.

00:18:10.020 --> 00:18:11.230
Look! An arm!

00:18:12.360 --> 00:18:14.070
Can you tell
if the pilot's okay?

00:18:14.440 --> 00:18:15.280
Not yet.

00:18:18.320 --> 00:18:22.120
I can get to him
as soon as I move this thing.

00:18:24.950 --> 00:18:25.870
Don't!

00:18:29.790 --> 00:18:30.540
Ota!

00:18:30.670 --> 00:18:32.630
- What's wrong, Noa?
- Ota is...

00:18:32.750 --> 00:18:34.840
Don't worry!
Get him out, fast!

00:18:34.880 --> 00:18:35.670
Okay.

00:18:36.420 --> 00:18:38.050
I can't!
His hips are buried!

00:18:38.420 --> 00:18:41.050
Forget the machine!
Get the cockpit!

00:18:41.050 --> 00:18:42.390
- But...
- Hurry!

00:18:42.600 --> 00:18:43.640
I can't hold this for long!

00:18:51.150 --> 00:18:53.770
- Is Ayano there?
- Yes.

00:18:54.020 --> 00:18:54.820
Put her on.

00:18:59.200 --> 00:19:01.990
I have a question for you.

00:19:03.530 --> 00:19:07.450
When you came to talk to me,
was it about this pilot?

00:19:08.750 --> 00:19:14.250
When you left me,
was it because of him?

00:19:16.670 --> 00:19:17.090
Yes.

00:19:18.340 --> 00:19:21.090
I understand. Thank you.

00:19:41.740 --> 00:19:42.950
I got him, Ota!

00:19:43.450 --> 00:19:45.660
Get him out!
It's giving way!

00:19:45.910 --> 00:19:46.870
Come on!

00:19:49.660 --> 00:19:50.620
Ota!

00:19:50.790 --> 00:19:52.460
Get out! Hurry!

00:20:09.390 --> 00:20:10.730
Noa, break open the cockpit!

00:20:11.060 --> 00:20:11.640
Roger.

00:20:16.060 --> 00:20:17.190
Takaaki!

00:20:22.950 --> 00:20:24.320
He's fine.
He's breathing.

00:20:24.910 --> 00:20:25.570
Ambulance!

00:20:30.950 --> 00:20:32.160
- Ota!
- Oh, no!

00:20:32.910 --> 00:20:33.670
Ota!

00:20:40.590 --> 00:20:42.130
Are you still alive?

00:20:42.220 --> 00:20:43.470
Of course!

00:20:48.470 --> 00:20:48.970
Noa...

00:22:07.840 --> 00:22:09.140
I can't believe this!

00:22:09.510 --> 00:22:13.260
They postponed it.
There's too much snow.

00:22:13.430 --> 00:22:14.520
What can we do?

00:22:14.680 --> 00:22:20.100
So what? We should practice in
all weather, under all conditions!

00:22:20.730 --> 00:22:23.780
That's our duty as police officers!

00:22:24.400 --> 00:22:27.990
We can fulfill our duty when
they reopen the training ground.

00:22:28.110 --> 00:22:29.820
You sure are persistent.

00:22:29.820 --> 00:22:33.030
Captain, where are you going?

00:22:33.240 --> 00:22:35.870
I want to have target practice!

00:22:35.870 --> 00:22:38.830
Now! Let's do it now! Captain!

00:22:43.340 --> 00:22:46.550
dakishimete MIDNIGHT BLUE
Just hold me tightly, Midnight Blue

00:22:46.670 --> 00:22:50.260
